      "stem": "A secured agent has the required runtime roles. Search resolves to a public IP from the agent network even though public access is disabled. The private endpoint exists. What should be investigated next?",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "The Search role assignments on the identity used by the deployment pipeline."
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "The query-time semantic ranking configuration on the target index."
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "The private endpoint connection approval state for the runtime subnet."
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "Private DNS resolution and links for the agent network."
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "D",
      "difficulty": "medium",
      "type": "single_choice",
      "explanation": {
        "whyCorrect": "A private endpoint must be reachable through correct DNS resolution and routing from the runtime network. Roles cannot repair resolution to a blocked public endpoint.",
        "whyDistractorsWrong": {
          "C": "The stated failure is name resolution to a public address.",
          "A": "The problem is name resolution from the runtime network.",
          "B": "Ranking is evaluated after a request reaches Search."
        }
      },
